                <pb facs="0935" n="855" sameAs="frus:frus1936v01/pg855"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.48A6 Liquor/10: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at Capetown</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">De Courcy</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-07-18T12:00:00-04:00">July 18,
                            1936—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">New York Times</hi> carries a story under a Capetown
                    dateline to the effect that the South African Wine Growers Association is
                    exhorting its members to buy British automobiles, machinery and household
                    appliances because of its disappointment at being unable to sell South African
                    wines in the United States. It is said that the Association has been trying to
                    enter the American market since the end of prohibition, but has been defeated by
                    the regulations and supplementary regulations which made it impossible to sell a
                    single bottle. It is reported that last week the Association had to cancel a
                    sample consignment at the last minute owing to the publication of more
                    supplementary regulations and that the Association now announces it is closing
                    its New York office.</p>
                <p>Please investigate and report briefly by telegram whether instances of this
                    nature have come to your attention.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
